  <h3>The MSP Channel</h3>
  <p>In the US, many SMBs outsource IT to MSPs (Managed Service Providers). Any US strategy must account for the MSP channel:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Tool</th><th>What it is</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>ConnectWise</strong></td><td>RMM + PSA + ITAM</td><td>Dominates the MSP channel</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Kaseya/Datto</strong></td><td>RMM + PSA</td><td>Second largest, aggressive acquisitions</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>NinjaOne</strong></td><td>RMM + endpoint mgmt</td><td>Explosive growth, modern UX</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Atera</strong></td><td>All-in-one IT mgmt</td><td>Per-technician pricing, popular with small MSPs</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>These are RMM/PSA tools, not ITAM with full lifecycle — but they cover part of the problem and MSPs already use them.</p>

